---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii4_238",
  "series": "Band II 4 (1701 - 1707)",
  "seq": 238,
  "text": "<p> [[715.21]] <b>238. LEIBNIZ AN BARTHÉLEMY DES BOSSES</p>\n<p> [[715.22]] Hannover, 24. Dezember 1707. [237.] </b></p>\n<p> [[716.3]] Admodum Reverende Pater, Fautor Honoratissime </p>\n<p> [[716.4]] Magna <Fn><i>Am Kopf von L^#'2 von Leibniz' Hand</i>: Au R. P. des Bosses Jesuite à Hildesheim 24 X^#'b^#'r 1707</Fn> spe decidi, non secuto adventu Tuo. Mitto ecce tandem librum Thomae Bonartis\n[[716.5]] expectoque ut ubi vacaverit, sententiam aliquando Tuam mihi de eo exponas. Sed inprimis\n[[716.6]] nomen viri et fortunam beneficio Tuo nosse optem. </p>\n<p> [[716.7]] Exscriptor noster sophistam non ineptum egit. Vetustior Codex non describendi, sed\n[[716.8]] describentem juvandi causa additus erat. Nolo tamen rigide uti jure meo, itaque ubi descriptionem\n[[716.9]] absolverit, dabitur adhuc quod jam descripti pretio proportione respondeat; quod ex\n[[716.10]] numero foliorum absolutorum et residuorum aestimari potest. </p>\n<p> [[716.11]] Versus satyrici quos misisti, non sunt inelegantes. Recte ne an secus ad Rempium applicentur\n[[716.12]] non dixerim nec nosse curo. Neque enim scripta ejus polemica legi aut lego. </p>\n<p> [[716.13]] Hartsoekerus, cujus opiniones ex R. P. Orbani literis memoras, videtur mihi ita sentire ut\n[[716.14]] hodie multi eruditorum in Batavis solent. Ingenio non caret, sed de plerisque phaenomenis\n[[716.15]] naturae judicat tumultuarie ut sic dicam, quadam condendi systematis physici ambitione, cui\n[[716.16]] nostrae notitiae nondum sunt satis maturae. Praeterea profundior Mathesis pariter et Metaphysica\n[[716.17]] ni fallor non est ad ejus palatum. </p>\n<p> [[716.18]] Ignosce quaeso quod elegantem librum inscriptum, <i>esprit des nouveaux disciples de\n[[717.1]] S. Augustin</i>, nondum remitto. Impedimenta intervenerant, quo minus lectionem absolverem.\n[[717.2]] Faciam tamen quamprimum. </p>\n<p> [[717.3]] Gratias ago quod Excerptum Peresii sane ingeniosum mihi misisti. Optime judicavit\n[[717.4]] Perezius, incrementum caritatis novum quod ipsa meretur caritas, non esse ejusdem cum ipsa\n[[717.5]] dimensionis. Si fuisset versatus in meo calculo infinitesimali dixisset incrementa esse infinite\n[[717.6]] parva vel infinitesima respectu caritatis quae [ea] meretur. Notandum est cum incrementa in\n[[717.7]] gravibus descendentibus quovis momento sint aequalia, hoc loco caritatis incrementa esse\n[[717.8]] ipsamet continue crescentia. <Fn><i>Dazu zeichnet Leibniz im Auszug</i>:  </Fn> Nam major caritas etiam majus meretur augmentum. Itaque\n[[717.9]] lineam quae velocitates gravis ad quodvis temporis momentum repraesentat esse rectam, sed\n[[717.10]] lineam quae caritates completas quovis momento acquisitas repraesentaret (fingendo augmentum\n[[717.11]] non interruptum) fore curvam, cujus constructio penderet ex Logarithmis. </p>\n<p> [[717.12]] Saepe dixi ad eos qui non nisi recentioris philosophiae sectatores probant, non esse\n[[717.13]] prorsus spernendos Scholasticos, saepeque in eorum luto aurum latere: ut adeo operae pretium\n[[717.14]] ingens facturus sit, qui selecta inde in usum publicum aliquando congeret. </p>\n<p> [[717.15]] Doleo deesse Theologiae et Philosophiae Scholasticae historiam; et vellem oriretur aliquando,\n[[717.16]] qui quae Petavius et Tomasinus de dogmatis Theologicis coepere ex patribus, ex\n[[717.17]] scholasticis absolveret. Ita Historiam dogmatum ad nostra usque tempora nancisceremur. </p>\n<p> [[717.18]] Nihilne amplius de Ptolemaeo vestro intelligimus? Quod superest vale et fave. Dabam\n[[717.19]] Hanoverae 24 X^#'b^#'r 1707. </p>\n<p> [[717.20]] G. G. Leibnitius </p>\n<p> [[718.1]] P. S. Instantem annum cum multis aliis faustum et felicem precor. <Fn><i>Darunter notiert Leibniz als Verweis auf das 2. P. S. auf Bl. 58 v^#'o</i> : vertatur si placet</Fn> </p>\n<p> [[718.2]] P. S. Nuper forte inter schedas occurrit, quod mihi communicasti ex chartis Monasterii\n[[718.3]] Heinigensis. Equidem multas Tibi eo nomine gratias debeo, sed quod ibi narratur, haud dubie\n[[718.4]] fictitium est, et ab omni Historia alienum. </p>\n<p> [[718.5]] Suppositiones ejusmodi faciunt, ut quidam etiam de genuinis dubitent, quemadmodum\n[[718.6]] hypocritae faciunt, ut multi nullum sincere pium credant. Hoc vitio laborat Germonius cum suis\n[[718.7]] Trivultianis amicis, qui omnia diplomata Carolinae familiae [videntur] rejicere, in quo valde\n[[718.8]] excedunt mensuram boni critici. Ego ipse nuper Cassellis genuinum Caroli M. diploma vidi\n[[718.9]] datum secundo imperii anno.\n [[719.2 ANHANG\n\n",
  "number": "238.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN BARTHÉLEMY DES BOSSES",
  "date": "Hannover, 24. Dezember 1707. [237.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:238. LEIBNIZ AN BARTHÉLEMY DES BOSSES Hannover, 24. Dezember 1707. [237.] Admodum Reverende Pater, Fautor Honoratissime Magna Am Kopf von L^#'2 von Leibniz' Hand: Au R. P. des Bosses Jesuite à Hildesheim 24 X^#'b^#'r 1707 spe decidi, non secuto adventu Tuo. Mitto ecce tandem librum Thomae Bonartis e...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>